  "text": "**Assessment: none of the three answers can be confirmed, so I answer NONE.**\n\n**Layer groups.** Solution 1's count of 34 is a lower bound, not a verified total:\n- Layer groups without a pure in-plane mirror σ_h embed in the wallpaper groups, so they give at most 17 abstract types. All 17 occur, since each wallpaper group W can be embedded with trivial z-action.\n- Layer groups with σ_h give extensions of W by a central Z₂. Taking W × ⟨σ_h⟩ for each W gives 17 more types. These are distinct from the wallpaper types because they have a nontrivial finite normal subgroup, which wallpaper groups lack.\n- Solution 1 then assumes every σ_h-containing layer group splits as W × Z₂. I did not verify that. A non-split central extension would add classes, which would push the count above 34.\n\nSo the layer count is at least 34, and 34 is the answer only if every σ_h-containing layer group splits.\n\n**Rod groups.** Solution 1's breakdown into 13 Z-type and 19 D∞-type classes is plausible in structure, but I could not check the individual assignments of the 75 groups. Solutions 2 and 3 give (61, 68) and (57, 63) with no derivation, and I cannot verify either.\n\nI have no reliable recollection of a published count that settles this, so I cannot identify which answer, if any, matches the literature.\n\nCHOICE: NONE",
